task_id: sql_0028
task_type: sql
instruction: "The SQLite database 'Database for tasks.sqlite3' in the current directory has tables: CATEGORY(WARE, CLASS) - which category (CLASS) a ware belongs to (a ware may belong to several categories); MANUFACTURER(BILL_ID, COMPANY) - bills of materials and the companies owning them; MATERIAL(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT) - materials used by a bill; PRODUCT(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT, PRICE) - wares produced by a bill, with amount and price. A bill may produce several wares. For each company show all the production chains (separate row per company/chain). The production chain is the intermediate product (ware) that is a product of one bill of the company and a material of another bill of the same company. Each chain must be presented in the form (MATERIAL1,MATERIAL2)-[BILL_ID1]->(INTERMEDIATE_PRODUCT)-[BILL_ID2]->(PRODUCT1,PRODUCT2). Chains where the first bill has no materials are skipped. Write one row per line as company;(MATERIAL1,MATERIAL2)-[BILL_ID1]->(INTERMEDIATE_PRODUCT)-[BILL_ID2]->(PRODUCT1,PRODUCT2). Inside parentheses the values are separated with comma (no spaces) and sorted alphabetically. Sort rows by company name first, then by the whole chain string. Compute the answer with bash (sqlite3 and/or python3). Work only inside the current directory. When you are done, write ONLY the final answer to the file answer.txt in the current directory (for example with bash: echo 42 > answer.txt)."
reward: 2
